    {
      "id": "04",
      "source_unit": "if-else",
      "title": "Equal Numbers",
      "difficulty": 1,
      "sidebar_tag": "if/else",
      "description": [
        "<p>Read two integers <code>a</code> and <code>b</code>, one per line, and",
        "print <code>Equal</code> if they're the same, or <code>Not Equal</code>",
        "otherwise. Use <code>==</code> to check equality &mdash; a single",
        "<code>=</code> is for assignment, not comparison.</p>",
        "<pre>&gt; python program.py",
        "3",
        "3",
        "Equal</pre>"
      ],
      "starter": [
        "a = int(input())",
        "b = int(input())",
        "",
        "# TODO: print \"Equal\" if a == b, otherwise \"Not Equal\""
      ],
      "tests": [
        {
          "stdin": [
            "3",
            "3"
          ],
          "expected": "Equal"
        },
        {
          "stdin": [
            "5",
            "7"
          ],
          "expected": "Not Equal"
        },
        {
          "stdin": [
            "0",
            "0"
          ],
          "expected": "Equal"
        },
        {
          "stdin": [
            "-2",
            "2"
          ],
          "expected": "Not Equal"
        },
        {
          "stdin": [
            "10",
            "9"
          ],
          "expected": "Not Equal"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "05",
      "source_unit": "if-else",
      "title": "Bigger Number",
      "difficulty": 2,
      "sidebar_tag": "if/elif/else",
      "description": [
        "<p>Read two integers <code>a</code> and <code>b</code>, one per line, and",
        "print which one is bigger &mdash; or that they're equal. This needs three",
        "possible outcomes, so it needs an <code>elif</code> (short for \"else",
        "if\") between the <code>if</code> and the <code>else</code>.</p>",
        "<pre>&gt; python program.py",
        "10",
        "3",
        "First is bigger</pre>",
        "<p>Python checks each condition in order and runs the first one that's",
        "true, skipping the rest &mdash; only one branch ever runs.</p>"
      ],
      "starter": [
        "a = int(input())",
        "b = int(input())",
        "",
        "# TODO: print \"First is bigger\", \"Second is bigger\", or \"They are equal\""
      ],
      "tests": [
        {
          "stdin": [
            "10",
            "3"
          ],
          "expected": "First is bigger"
        },
        {
          "stdin": [
            "3",
            "10"
          ],
          "expected": "Second is bigger"
        },
        {
          "stdin": [
            "5",
            "5"
          ],
          "expected": "They are equal"
        },
        {
          "stdin": [
            "-1",
            "-5"
          ],
          "expected": "First is bigger"
        },
        {
          "stdin": [
            "0",
            "0"
          ],
          "expected": "They are equal"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
