    {
      "id": "08",
      "source_unit": "if-else",
      "title": "Temperature Category",
      "difficulty": 1,
      "sidebar_tag": "elif chain",
      "description": [
        "<p>Read a <code>temp</code> (in Fahrenheit) and print a category using this",
        "scale:</p>",
        "<pre>below 32   &rarr; Freezing",
        "32&ndash;59      &rarr; Cold",
        "60&ndash;79      &rarr; Warm",
        "80 and above &rarr; Hot</pre>",
        "<pre>&gt; python program.py",
        "45",
        "Cold</pre>",
        "<p>Since Python checks conditions top to bottom and stops at the first true",
        "one, the order you write these branches in matters &mdash; a broader",
        "condition placed too early can accidentally catch cases meant for a later",
        "branch.</p>"
      ],
      "starter": [
        "# TODO: read a temperature, then print its category",
        "# (Freezing, Cold, Warm, or Hot) using the scale above"
      ],
      "tests": [
        {
          "stdin": [
            "20"
          ],
          "expected": "Freezing"
        },
        {
          "stdin": [
            "45"
          ],
          "expected": "Cold"
        },
        {
          "stdin": [
            "70"
          ],
          "expected": "Warm"
        },
        {
          "stdin": [
            "95"
          ],
          "expected": "Hot"
        },
        {
          "stdin": [
            "32"
          ],
          "expected": "Cold"
        }
      ]
    },
